          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            By a
            %em finite rotation group
            one means a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite"} finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subgroup"} subgroup
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rotations"} rotations
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/special+orthogonal+group"} special orthogonal group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(n)
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spin+group"} spin group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(n)
            or similar.
          %p
            The finite subgroups of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SO%283%29"} SO(3)
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SU%282%29"} SU(2)
            follow an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ADE+classification"} ADE classification
            (theorem
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClassificationOfFiniteSubgroupsOfSO3"}
            below).
          %h2#classifications Classifications
          %h3#finite_subgroups_of___and_
            Finite subgroups of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
