          %h2#References References
          %h3#finite_subgroups_of__and_
            Finite subgroups of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi SO
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SO(3)
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spin
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 3
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spin(3)
          %p
            The classification in Theorem
            %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#ClassificationOfFiniteSubgroupsOfSO3"}
            goes back to
          %ul
            %li#Klein1884
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Felix+Klein"}> Felix Klein
              , chapter I of
              = succeed "," do
                %em Vorlesungen über das Ikosaeder und die Auflösung der Gleichungen vom fünften Grade
              %em Lectures on the Icosahedron and the Resolution of Equations of Degree Five
              by George Morrice 1888,
              %a{:href => "https://archive.org/details/cu31924059413439"} online version
          %p
            Expository review of the argument in
            = succeed ":" do
              %a{:href => "#Klein1884"} Klein 1884
          %ul
            %li#Senechal90
              Marjorie Senechal,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Finding the Finite Groups of Symmetries of the Sphere
              %strong 97
              4 (1990) 329-335 (
              %a{:href => "https://www.jstor.org/stable/2324519"}> jstor:2324519
              )
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li#MillerBlichfeldtDickson16
              %p
                G. A. Miller, H. F. Blichfeldt,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonard+E.+Dickson"} Leonard E. Dickson
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Theory and applications of finite groups
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://archive.org/details/theoryapplicatio00milluoft/"} ark:/13960/t0ht2kb4x
            %li#Lamotke86
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Klaus+Lamotke"}> Klaus Lamotke
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Regular Solids and Isolated Singularities
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://link.springer.com/book/10.1007/978-3-322-91767-6"} doi:10.1007/978-3-322-91767-6
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mark+A.+Armstrong"}> Mark A. Armstrong
                , chapter 19 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Groups and Symmetry
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-1-4757-4034-9"} doi:10.1007/978-1-4757-4034-9
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://superoles.wordpress.com/wp-content/uploads/2014/10/lluvia.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Rees05
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Elmer+Rees"}> Elmer Rees
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Notes on Geometry
          %p see also
          %ul
            %li#Serrano14
              Javier Carrasco Serrano,
              = succeed "," do
                %em
                  Finite subgroups of
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi SL
